-- FINDING 8 (loud).  The TIMEZONE that TODAY needs is the one in the module that EVALUATES, not the one in the
-- module that defines the rule.  f08a declares TIMEZONE and reads TODAY; this module imports f08a and, with no
-- TIMEZONE of its own, gets an error at each directive.  Printed: an error per #EVAL, "TIMEZONE is not declared.
-- TODAY requires 'TIMEZONE IS "<IANA timezone>"' in your document."  Every module in the row that evaluates
-- (tests, seat) therefore declares TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore".
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `f08a-timezone-library`

#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 8 2012) `the day the law is read`
